/P 1422 0 R
/E (A majority of students enrolled in Entrepreneurship \(ENT\) courses are from the Economics Department, followed by Computer Science and then Psychology, highlighting diverse classroom dynamics. Among 83 respondents, 33% selected Entrepreneurship as a Minor/Concentration highlighting the popularity of CfE among the students. However, many students felt the need for more representation of students from other departments to enrich classroom experience.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [11]
>>
